new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a7cdca3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/SECURITY_DEPLOYMENT.md
@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+# 67 Superadmin + GitHub Module — Production Deployment
+
+The Superadmin/GitHub control plane is fail-closed: privileged authentication is unavailable until every required production secret and origin setting is valid. The implementation uses Node.js built-ins only; this patch adds no runtime npm dependency.
+
+## Required deployment controls
+
+1. Run the Node service on `127.0.0.1` behind HTTPS. Set `SUPERADMIN_ALLOWED_ORIGIN` to the exact public origin, with no trailing slash/path/query.
+2. Generate the Superadmin scrypt hash interactively with `npm run admin:hash-password`; the utility disables terminal echo. Put the result in the secret manager/environment as `SUPERADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH`.
+3. Generate independent values for `SUPERADMIN_SESSION_SECRET` (32+ bytes) and `SUPERADMIN_ENCRYPTION_KEY` (exactly 32 bytes after base64 decode). Never reuse either value as a password or GitHub token.
+4. Keep `DATA_DIR` outside the Git checkout, owner-only (`0700`). Secret/config and audit files are written as `0600` where supported. The GitHub token and sensitive Superadmin profile fields are AES-256-GCM encrypted at rest with separate AAD contexts.
+5. `GIT_REPOSITORY_ROOT` must be the exact trusted checkout. Its single `origin` fetch URL and single push URL must identify the same github.com repository selected in Superadmin.
+6. Prefer a fine-grained GitHub token restricted to the one repository and minimum required permissions. For the strongest deployment, inject `GITHUB_TOKEN` from a server secret manager; environment-managed tokens cannot be removed from the UI.
+7. Run the service as a dedicated non-root OS account. Do not share that OS account with untrusted shell users or unrelated workloads.
+8. Set `TRUST_PROXY=1` only when exactly one trusted reverse proxy is in front of Node and that proxy overwrites (not appends user-controlled values to) `X-Forwarded-For` and `X-Forwarded-Proto`.
+9. Back up the encrypted state only under a policy that separately protects the encryption key. Losing the key makes encrypted GitHub/profile data intentionally unreadable.
+10. Treat repository code and its `npm test` / `npm run build` scripts as trusted deployment code. The GitHub gate scrubs child-process environment secrets and disables Git hooks/filters, but build/test scripts are project code and should run inside the dedicated service account or an isolated container/VM.
+
+## GitHub execution guardrails
+
+- GitHub API and Git network targets are restricted to official GitHub HTTPS endpoints; SSH/git/file/ext protocols are disabled for controlled operations.
+- Git credentials are supplied through a temporary private `GIT_ASKPASS` helper; tokens are not embedded in remote URLs or returned to the browser.
+- Local Git configuration capable of executing commands, injecting credentials/headers, changing TLS trust, adding includes, filters, helpers, proxies, hooks, submodules or alternate transports is rejected.
+- `.env`, credentials, keys, database dumps, archives, logs, uploads/runtime directories, `.github/workflows`, symlinks and submodules are blocked from controlled pushes.
+- Outgoing commits are audited, not only the current working tree. A secret added in an older outgoing commit and deleted later is still blocked. Outgoing merge commits require manual review.
+- Review authorization is HMAC-signed, bound to the active Superadmin session, exact repository/branch/action/push mode, reviewed HEAD/remote SHA, file count and content/mode manifest, and expires within 10 minutes.
+- For pushes, `npm test` and `npm run build` must both pass before authorization is issued.
+- After staging, Git blob IDs and modes are rechecked against the reviewed manifest. The push uses the exact reviewed/generated commit SHA rather than a moving `HEAD`. A concurrent remote change is rejected by normal non-force Git push semantics.
+
+## Superadmin web controls
+
+- Server-side password verification (scrypt), single active server session, signed HttpOnly/Secure/SameSite=Strict cookie, CSRF token, exact production Origin checks, rate limits and audit logging.
+- No default admin username/password/OTP/bypass is embedded in the frontend.
+- Sensitive bank/profile settings are stored encrypted server-side instead of `localStorage`.
+- Privileged endpoints require HTTPS in production. Security headers prevent framing and unsafe cross-origin control-plane use while retaining same-origin camera/microphone/geolocation/payment capability used by the wider app; the existing Google Maps embed is explicitly allowed.
+
+## Build and deploy gate
+
+```bash
+npm ci
+npm test
+npm run build
+NODE_ENV=production npm start
+```
+
+Health check: `GET /api/health`.
+
+The application does **not** parse `.env` files automatically; inject variables with systemd/PM2/container/orchestrator secrets/environment. This avoids adding a dotenv dependency and prevents accidental secret-file loading from the Git checkout.
+
+## Reverse proxy baseline
+
+Proxy `/` to `http://127.0.0.1:4173`, terminate TLS at the proxy, set `Host`, overwrite `X-Forwarded-For` with the trusted proxy chain policy, and set `X-Forwarded-Proto https`. Do not expose port 4173 publicly.
+
+## Existing platform scope
+
+This patch preserves the original 67 Superadmin business dashboard and adds the GitHub Module to it while replacing its demo authentication and sensitive profile storage. Existing seller/customer/payment/document/community dashboard records in the supplied 67 frontend are still mock/client-side demo data from the original project; this patch does not invent a production business database for those pre-existing modules. They require a separate backend/data migration before those records can be considered production source-of-truth.
